{"author":"schacon+claude-opus@gmail.com","body":"894b119cc (push.rs logic) + 69aa276e2 (push_submodules.rs/toml/log); 29/29 passing (was 21/29). Root causes: (1) --no-recurse-submodules applied before config so config re-enabled recursion -> now config baseline, cmdline tokens, then --no-recurse last; (2) collect_changed_gitlinks_for_push fell back to destination heads pruning the super walk so on-demand skipped submodule when super ref already up to date -> removed fallback, matches --not --remotes=<name>; (3) only-is-on-demand was forced as a mode -> now conditional only->on-demand transform; (4) nested_only derived from env so children of a top-level only push never got only-is-on-demand -> always true when recursing; (5) submodule remote/refspec propagation gated on path_style_remote instead of remote_is_configured_name (a local-path configured remote like origin must still propagate). NOTE: push.rs is shared with a concurrent porcelain agent that reverted my edits twice; my first commit captured a reverted push.rs, so 894b119cc re-applies the real logic - both commits needed."}